<script lang="ts">
	import Demo from "./demo.svelte";
</script>

# Progress

Shows how much of a task is complete, such as an upload. The indicator slides to the new amount when `value` changes. The root sets `role="progressbar"` with `aria-valuenow`, so give it an `aria-label` or point `aria-labelledby` at a visible label.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Progress } from "#lib/components/ui/progress/index.js";
</script>

<Progress value={33} aria-label="Upload progress" />
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/progress.json
```

## Max

Set `max` to measure progress in your own units, such as files or bytes. The default is `100`, and values outside `0` to `max` are clamped.

<Demo section="max" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Progress value={3} max={8} aria-label="Files uploaded" />
```

## Indeterminate

Omit `value` or pass `null` when the amount is unknown. A short indicator sweeps across the track, and it pulses in place instead when the user prefers reduced motion.

<Demo section="indeterminate" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Progress aria-label="Loading" />
```

## Variants

Set `variant` to `default` or `destructive`. The track uses a light tint of the indicator color.

<Demo section="variants" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Progress variant="destructive" value={33} aria-label="Storage used" />
```

## Sizes

Set `size` to `xs`, `sm`, `md`, or `lg` to change the bar thickness. The default is `sm`, and the corner radius follows the size.

<Demo section="sizes" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Progress size="lg" value={33} aria-label="Upload progress" />
```

## Rounded

Set `rounded` to `xs` through `4xl` or `pill` to override the radius from the size. Use `pill` for a pill.

<Demo section="rounded" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Progress size="md" rounded="pill" value={33} aria-label="Upload progress" />
```

## API

The `Progress` props extend the native `div` attributes. Extra attributes, such as `aria-label`, pass through to the root. The root also sets `data-state` to `indeterminate`, `loading`, or `complete` for custom styles.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface Props extends CompProps<"div"> {
	/** Completed amount from `0` to `max`; omit or pass `null` for indeterminate */
	value?: number | null;
	/** Amount that counts as complete; defaults to `100` */
	max?: number;
	/** Visual style of the track and indicator */
	variant?: "default" | "destructive";
	/** Bar thickness on the shared scale; defaults to `sm` */
	size?: UiSize;
	/** Corner radius; follows `size` when omitted */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
}
```
